I used the instructions by @yonie1 above (thanks!) and now switched to the "official" sensors. This is how I did it.

Lookup the `metadata_id` of the manually created "Energy from Grid" sensor (OLD_ID):
```sql
SELECT id FROM statistics_meta WHERE statistic_id='sensor.energy_from_grid';
```

Lookup the `metadata_id` of the new official sensors (NEW_ID):
```sql
SELECT id FROM statistics_meta WHERE statistic_id='sensor.positive_active_energy_total';
```

Substitute OLD_ID and NEW_ID and run the following queries (**but make a backup first, really!**):
```sql
DELETE FROM statistics_short_term WHERE metadata_id=NEW_ID;
UPDATE statistics_short_term SET metadata_id=NEW_ID WHERE metadata_id=OLD_ID;
DELETE FROM statistics WHERE metadata_id=NEW_ID;
UPDATE statistics SET metadata_id=NEW_ID WHERE metadata_id=OLD_ID;
```
As a last step, go to your Energy dashboard settings and select the new sensors.

(Repeat everything for "sensor.energy_to_grid" and "sensor.negative_active_energy_total" if you return energy to the grid, too.)
